# What the backend image is built without. Dockerfile.backend copies
# requirements.txt, alembic.ini, alembic/ and backend/ by name, so nothing
# else in the repository reaches the image whatever this file says. The
# patterns that still decide something are the ones for what can sit INSIDE
# those two directories; they start with `**/`, because a pattern without it
# is matched at the top of the build context and nowhere below.

# Python: what the interpreter and its tools leave beside a module.
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/

# Database files, wherever one was made.
**/*.db
sql_app.db

# IDE / Editor
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Git
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Environment files, wherever one was left. backend/.env is the one that
# matters most: python-dotenv looks beside backend/database.py before it
# looks in /app, so the server would read a copy that got into the image.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Docs
*.md
LICENSE

# Frontend (not needed in backend image)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
